  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The single storey rear extension,  by reason of the excessive size in terms of depth, coupled with the choice of flat roof design, would form an overly dominant and an incongruous addition to the dwelling that would adversely impact on the character and appearance of the main building, the row of three terraced dwellings of which the application property forms a part, the Highfields Road rear streetscene and the surrounding area, contrary to Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan and the guidance in Supplementary Planning Document 'Design of Residential Extensions' (SPD4) and Sutton's Urban Design Guide 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places' SPD (SPD14).",
    "The proposal, due to its excessive depth, coupled with flat roof and high eaves line in immediate proximity to neighbouring boundaries and rear and side amenity areas of No. 55 Highfield Road and primary rear windows of the first floor flat at 53A Highfield Road, would create a sense of enclosure and would unacceptably compromise the visual amenity and outlook currently enjoyed from the rear and side outdoor areas of No. 55 Highfield Road, as well as from the primary rear windows servicing the first floor flat at No. 53A Highfield Road directly above the proposed extension. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed kitchen extractor will be situated within close proximity of the primary bedroom windows of the first floor flat at 53A Highfield Road and the adjacent 51 Highfield Road, and without evidence to the contrary, would adversely impact the amenity of the occupiers of these properties through unacceptable increase of noise and disturbance, and odours, contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
